  "lineage": "French opera genre in which spoken dialogue alternates with sung numbers, grown from the plays with songs of the eighteenth-century Paris fair theatres and identified with the Opéra-Comique company, housed at the Salle Favart from 1783. Grétry, Boieldieu, Hérold, Auber and Adam shaped its romances, couplets and ensembles, and by the later nineteenth century the term also covered serious works such as Bizet's Carmen, premiered there with spoken dialogue in 1875. The generic strings and flute cards stand in for the orchestra's string section and flutes.",
